.TH XD\-TASKMGR 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-taskmgr \- Task Manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-taskmgr
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-taskmgr
is the Windows 2000 Task Manager, with Windows XP's Networking and Users
tabs:
.TP
.B Applications
The open windows: End Task, Switch To and New Task.
.TP
.B Processes
Every process, with selectable columns: End Process, End Process Tree,
Set Priority and Set Affinity.
.TP
.B Performance
CPU and memory meters, history graphs and totals, in Linux terms
(committed memory is
.BR Committed_AS ;
kernel memory is the reclaimable and unreclaimable slab).
.TP
.B Networking
A graph per network adapter.
.TP
.B Users
The logind sessions, with Logoff and Disconnect.
.PP
Ctrl+Shift+Esc (and Ctrl+Alt+Delete in the XP and 7 styles) opens it, or
brings the running one forward.
While it runs, its CPU meter sits in the notification area.
Process data comes from procps-ng's libproc2.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show GApplication's summary of options and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-compositor (1),
.BR xd\-security (1),
.BR ps (1)
